<title>ZIMBABWE: Four people killed in Zimbabwe aircrash.</title>
<headline>Four people killed in Zimbabwe aircrash.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four people were killed on Sunday when a light aircraft plunged in Lake Kariba in northern Zimbabwe soon after take-off, the state-owned Herald newspaper reported on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the Cessna 210, with four people on board, crashed at a bay some 500 metres (yards) from the airstrip it had taken off.</p>
<p>A police spokesman said all four bodies had been retrieved from the lake, and investigations were going on into the cause of the accident.</p>
</text>
